# Dynamic Import Safety

- Prefer static imports so missing modules and bad exports fail early during typecheck and build, not only at runtime.
- Avoid `import()` in application and server code by default.
- Do not use dynamic imports as a workaround for typing, module-resolution, or environment issues.

## Allowed narrow exceptions

- Explicit framework-level code splitting such as route or component lazy loading.
- Truly optional integrations where loading must depend on runtime availability.

## When an exception is used

- Add a short inline comment explaining why a static import is not appropriate.
- Keep the dynamic import at the narrowest possible scope.
- Prefer one well-justified dynamic import over spreading the pattern through the codebase.
